  "summary": "Five Euclid DR1 papers appeared on 12 November 2026, documenting the release contents, survey coverage, masks, photometry validation and PHZ galaxy properties.",
  "synthesis": "The items form a coordinated documentation set for Euclid Data Release 1 rather than a set of cosmological analyses. The overview describes a two-part release of images, spectra and catalogues covering about a billion objects from wide and deep fields, while the survey paper reports 2100 deg² of Wide Survey area. Supporting papers describe the photometric masks, which trace spatial variations in survey properties, and the PHZ pipeline, which applies NNPZ nearest-neighbour inference with a COSMOS reference sample to derive non-cosmological galaxy properties. The main quantified check is the multi-band photometry comparison with the JWST-based COSMOS2025 catalogue, where median offsets are mostly within 10% and largest in NIR deep model-fitting. None of the items presents cosmological results.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
